  "findings": [
    "The prior sustained-below-tls-2 cohort retained all eight required revisits at 24.750717005 to 26.723728704 seconds. The current cohort retained four revisits at 25.089437554 to 27.627562826 seconds and lost four at 30.915823195 to 31.252490421 seconds.",
    "For each of the four changed outcomes, the prior put-idle to current request-start interval is below 30 seconds in the prior run and above 30 seconds in the current run. Expiry therefore occurs before the new connection GotConn delay and is not an artifact of adding connection establishment time to the reported idle age.",
    "The sum of the three intervening measured transfer wall durations increased by 4.273828342 to 4.977530014 seconds for the four changed lanes. The remaining non-wall interval changed by less than 0.2 seconds. This directly accounts for the policy-boundary crossing at the harness level.",
    "This comparison explains why conditioning differs from the prior valid sustained cohort. It does not explain why the intervening transfers were slower and does not support changing the 30-second policy, rerunning the cohort, or changing runtime behavior."
  ],
